            <div xml:id="d1772">

                <pb facs="1158" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1042"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/37.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your despatch No. 69,
                    dated January 16, 1914, and to the Department’s telegram of January 29, there is
                    enclosed herewith, for your information, a copy of a letter dated November 22,
                    1913, from the Navy Department to the Secretary of State, in regard to the
                    proposed agreement between the United States and Panama concerning the
                    establishment of radio telegraph stations in the Republic of Panama.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to communicate the recommendations of the Joint Board to the
                    Government of Panama as a basis for the proposed agreement, and to report fully
                    to the Department the views of the Panaman Government with reference to the
                    different points mentioned in the recommendations of the Joint Board.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
